<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#taoiseach">Glossary</a> · Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Taoiseach</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Taoiseach is the head of government of Ireland, nominated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dail-eireann">Dáil Éireann</a> and appointed by the President. The office was created by the Constitution of 1937, replacing the President of the Executive Council of the Irish Free State, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eamon-de-valera">Éamon de Valera</a> was the first to hold it. The word means 'chief' or 'leader' in Irish.</p></div>
